'''belsire†''' (bel′sīr), ''n.'' [< ME. ''belsire'', lit. good sire, < ''bel'', fair, good, as a prefix, grand- (as in ''beldam'', q. v.), + ''sire''. Cf. ''beausire''.] '''1.''' A grandfather: correlative to ''beldam'', grandmother.—'''2.''' An ancestor. ''Drayton.''

'''belswagger†''' (bel′swag″ėr), ''n.'' [Perhaps for ''belly-swagger'', a form given by Ash, < ''belly'' + ''swag'', sway.] A bully; a pimp.

'''belt''' (belt), ''n.'' [< ME. ''belt'', < AS. ''belt'' = OHG. ''balz'' = Icel. ''belti'' = Sw. ''bälte'' = Dan. ''bælte'' =

